{
    ?: (Yes; Yeah, of course.)
        Plus, I have your VLID, and you're the only client I've had in the past 3 weeks.
        I'll know it's you if Asuracom comes knocking on my door.
        Don't think my team can't just as easily break your VI-LINK.
        |ARDA| Are you done threatening me so we can get on with it?
        |MAN| I'm not threatening you, just some... terms and conditions.
        |ARDA| Right... Moving on.
        || He smirks, though it's hard to tell if it's out of amusement or annoyance.
        |MAN| Moving on...
                What you're getting isn't a patch or plug-in. It's a permanent bypass.
                Burn once. Firmware update, you know how it goes.
    ?: (Questions; Can I ask some questions first?)
        |MAN| If it's anything technical, no, I don't make the mods.
        # This is a very messy way to configure a question loop, but it is possible!!!
        :SET asked_caught = false
        :SET asked_x = false
        :SET asked_y = false
        [skip:questionloop]
            |MAN| Any other questions?
        [/skip]
        {
            ?: [when:asked_caught=false] (Caught; What if I get caught with this thing?)
                :SET asked_caught = true
                |MAN| You never check the feeds? Or is this your idea of a joke?
                      Asuracom has an agreement with every country they serve.
                      Unauthorized VI-LINK modification is usually a federal offense and Fringe trespass is an aggravating circumstance.
                || He looks frustrated, almost to the point of suspicion; that'd you'd come in and ask him to explain the risks.
            ?: [when:asked_x=false] (Other; Some other question)
                :SET asked_x = true
                Some other answer.
            ?: [when:asked_y=false] (Another; A 3rd question)
                :SET asked_y = true
                A third answer.
            ?: No
                -> endloop
        }
        # Shows the re-ask prompt.
        [branch]
            [when:asked_caught=false]
                -> questionloop
        [/branch]
        [branch]
            [when:asked_x=false]
                -> questionloop
        [/branch]
        [branch]
            [when:asked_y=false]
                -> questionloop
        [/branch]        
        # Fallback when we run out of questions.
        |MAN| Alright, enough questions, I have other things to do today, kid.
        @endloop
        |MAN| The only other warning I got for you is that this is a permanent bypass.
              Burn once. Only way to get it to work.
}
